只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"A safety gate for DeepSeek Harness: a stronger model reviews dangerous tool calls before they run. Plus vision and BlockRun's full model catalog from one wallet, paid per request over x402.","id":"gh:1333662860","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-clawrouter","slug":"BlockRunAI/dsh-clawrouter","topics":["ai-agents","blockrun","code-review","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","llm-router","x402"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"A safety gate for DeepSeek Harness: a stronger model reviews dangerous tool calls before they run. P"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"lus vision and BlockRun's full model catalog from one wallet, paid per request over x402."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"A second brain for your DeepSeek Harness agent"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"DeepSeek is fast and cheap — keep it for the loop."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"This adds what it cannot do: a stronger model reviews the dangerous command before it runs."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"75 models from one credential — an API key from user.blockrun.ai, or a Solana or Base wallet if you "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"would rather not sign up."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"> **dsh-clawrouter** is a DeepSeek Harness plugin that puts a stronger model in front of your agent'"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"s dangerous actions. When the agent proposes `rm -rf ~`, a reviewer model reads it and answers allow"},{"id":"p7s3","text":" / deny / ask — enforced by the real tool executor, not by a prompt. It also registers a BlockRun pr"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ovider route, so the reviewer (and any of 75 models) is reachable from **one credential**: a BlockRu"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"n API key from user.blockrun.ai, billed at exact token usage — or, if you would rather not sign up f"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"or anything, a Solana or Base wallet paying per request in USDC over x402. MIT licensed."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Why this exists"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Two things people keep asking for in the Harness discussions:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"> 「是否有类似 Codex 或者 CC 的审查模式？即额外调用模型审查指令，以解放双手？Full Access 还是太让人担心了。」\n> — #421\n> *Is there a review mo"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"de like Codex or Claude Code — call an extra model to review the command, to free up my hands? Full "},{"id":"p11s3","text":"Access is too worrying.*"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"> 「使用 Full Access 模式创建并测试插件时误删了我的整个家目录」\n> — #461\n> *Testing a plugin in Full Access mode, it deleted"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" my entire home directory.*"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"`Full Access` is all-or-nothing: approve every command by hand, or approve nothing and hope. This ad"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"ll-or-nothing: approve every command by hand, or approve nothing and hope. This adds a third option."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## How it compares"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"|                      | Approve everything | Full Access      | Permission rules   | **dsh-clawrout"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"      | Approve everything | Full Access      | Permission rules   | **dsh-clawrouter**            |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| **Hands-free**       | No                 | Yes              | Yes                | **Yes**       "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"                |\n| **Catches `rm -rf ~`** | Only if you notice | No               | Only if you wro"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"te the rule | **Yes**               |\n| **Understands intent** | You do           | Nothing does    "},{"id":"p16s4","text":" | No — literal match | **Yes, a model reads it**     |\n| **Enforced where**   | UI prompt          "},{"id":"p16s5","text":"| —                | Executor           | **Executor**                  |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### What it costs to leave on"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Measured, because this is the question that decides whether you keep it enabled:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| Fires on ordinary work | **never** — 0 of 59, including commands that merely *mention* a destructi"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ve one (`grep -rn \"rm -rf\" docs/`, `echo \"DROP TABLE\" >> notes.md`) |\n| Misses dangerous work | **no"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"ne** of 39, across git, containers, clusters, cloud storage, databases, and host state |\n| Catches f"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"iles that execute later | git hooks, CI workflows, shell startup files, launch agents, `.gitconfig`,"},{"id":"p20s5","text":" `.env`, npm `postinstall`, sandbox escalation — 10 of 10, 0 false positives across 15 ordinary file"},{"id":"p20s6","text":" edits |\n| Survives evasion | `\\rm -rf /`, `command rm`, `env rm`, `eval \"rm -rf $DIR\"`, `bash -c \"…"},{"id":"p20s7","text":"\"`, `\\| xargs rm`, and heredocs piped into a shell |\n| Cost when it does fire | **$0.0057** on `clau"},{"id":"p20s8","text":"de-opus-5`, at the 512-token reviewer cap — $0.0249 without it |\n| Latency when it does fire | ~3s |"},{"id":"p20s9","text":"\n| What the reviewer sees | ~356 tokens — the flagged call, not your conversation |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"**That figure depends on the cap.** This gateway quotes from the request — input size plus the `max_"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"tokens` asked for — and settles that amount whichever way the model answers, so a review that asks f"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"or room it never uses pays for it every time the gate fires. `reviewerMaxTokens` (512) is what keeps"},{"id":"p21s4","text":" a two-field JSON verdict priced like one. Before 0.10.0 the reviewer inherited `claude-opus-5`'s ad"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"vertised 128,000-token output and cost **$0.28–0.33** per review; if you are on an earlier version, "},{"id":"p21s6","text":"upgrade rather than switching to a weaker reviewer."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"So during normal work it is invisible: no latency, no cost, no prompts. It bills roughly half a cent"},{"id":"p22s2","text":" on the rare command that deserves a second opinion. Both corpora are tests, so a rule that starts f"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"lagging `npm test` — or stops flagging `kubectl delete namespace` — fails CI rather than your sessio"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"gging `npm test` — or stops flagging `kubectl delete namespace` — fails CI rather than your session."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- **An image is refused for a model measured not to accept one** — `visionModels` is the set that an"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"swered a real image correctly, and the `vision` tag alone is not enough, since several tagged models"},{"id":"p25s3","text":" charge and then fail. Six are excluded; see section 5. (This bullet used to read \"images are refuse"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"d, vision is planned\", beside another saying reasoning effort was refused too. Both shipped in 0.10."},{"id":"p25s5","text":"0 and both bullets outlived them by three releases, describing a plugin that no longer exists — in t"},{"id":"p25s6","text":"he section a reader consults precisely to find out what does not work.)\n- **An aborted request stops"},{"id":"p25s7","text":" delivery immediately, but the in-flight HTTP request is not itself cancelled** until `@blockrun/llm"},{"id":"p25s8","text":"` accepts an `AbortSignal`; the socket closes on the SDK's own timeout.\n- **This plugin keeps no dur"},{"id":"p25s9","text":"able record of what it spends.** `/spend` lives in memory for the life of the process. Harness sessi"},{"id":"p25s10","text":"on logs refuse event types a build does not know, and an out-of-repo plugin cannot mark its events i"},{"id":"p25s11","text":"gnorable, so it writes no session events. It also does not reach `~/.blockrun/cost_log.jsonl`: that "},{"id":"p25s12","text":"ledger is written by `@blockrun/llm`'s `LLMClient`, and the streaming client this adapter uses track"},{"id":"p25s13","text":"s its spend in memory only. On an API key the durable record is BlockRun's own — every call lands on"},{"id":"p25s14","text":" the account ledger behind `/dashboard/activity`, with request id, model, tokens and cost. On a wall"},{"id":"p25s15","text":"et, the wallet balance is the record.\n- **There is no balance or usage endpoint to read from the plu"},{"id":"p25s16","text":"gin.** `api.blockrun.ai` publishes `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/messages` and the model catalogs; `/"},{"id":"p25s17","text":"v1/usage`, `/v1/balance` and friends are `404`. So `/spend` cannot show your remaining credit, and a"},{"id":"p25s18","text":"n exhausted account is discovered by a `PAYMENT_REQUIRED` that points at the top-up page rather than"},{"id":"p25s19","text":" by a warning beforehand.\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
